00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.920
Okay, so now what is exactly a magnitude analysis?

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.680
It's all about comparing the measure values across different categories and dimensions.

3
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.920
And this can help us of course to understand the importance of different categories.

4
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.079
Now the formula for that can be interesting.

5
00:00:18.079 --> 00:00:20.719
So now this time we will be mixing stuff together.

6
00:00:20.719 --> 00:00:23.879
So first we have to go and aggregate a specific measure.

7
00:00:23.879 --> 00:00:26.000
And then we say by dimension.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.219
We need here the dimension in order to split the measure.

9
00:00:29.219 --> 00:00:32.000
It sounds complicated, but it is very simple and basic.

10
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:37.540
So for example, we can say the total sales by country, the total quantity by category,

11
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.500
