12
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.540
And if you follow this formula, you will be generating endless amount of insights.

13
00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:50.459
By just combining any measure with any dimension, you can call it, it is a new insight.

14
00:00:50.459 --> 00:00:51.740
So it's going to look like this.

15
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.860
If you have one measure that is like, for example, 600, and if you put now this measure

16
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.259
together with the dimension, what can happen?

17
00:00:58.259 --> 00:01:01.259
This 600 is going to be split by the dimension values.

18
00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:05.419
So A can have like 200, B can have 300, and C 100.

19
00:01:05.419 --> 00:01:09.019
And now with that, we can go and compare those categories, right?

20
00:01:09.019 --> 00:01:13.860
So we can see now that category B has the highest measure and the C has the lowest.

21
00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.620
And this helps us to compare the values of the measure, what is the best category and

22
00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.319
what is the worst category.

23
00:01:19.319 --> 00:01:21.300
So this is very basic analysis.

